  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VCCI Can Tho</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to tackle inequality and human suffering in global seafood supply chains. It will continue to adopt Oxfam&#x2019;s multi-faceted global-to-local approach to ending human rights violations and addressing illegal and harmful fishing practices in global seafood supply chains. The project brings together Oxfam&#x2019;s flagship corporate advocacy efforts towards implementation and strategic engagement with investors and partners at the country level to ensure that global policy commitments are translated into change in supply chains. It will build upon significant progress and lessons in the previous grant Tackling Inequality and Human Suffering in Global Seafood Supply Chains (#2021-72284), with an increased focus on implementing changes at US companies, deeper engagement with Asian Seafood companies and an increased focus on empowering fishing communities and CSOs.
The project is funded and overallmanaged by Oxfam in Vietnam. Vietnam Chamber of Commerce and Industry Branch in Can Tho (VCCI Can Tho) will be in charge of implementing the project. After achieving approval from local authorities, VCCI Can Tho will cooperate with relevant government agencies, stakeholders and consultants to launch the activities. VCCI Can Tho will together with Oxfam to conduct monitoring and evaluation activities in accordance with the project document and expected outcomes. Besides, they will also support in organizing field trips to project sites and assign on-site staff to regular check the progress of the project as well as participate in activities to keep updating and promptly solve issues encountered during the project implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
